            <ArticleTitle>Cardiac gas embolism after central venous catheter removal.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>325-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Clinical images reporting intracardiac gas level are sparce and, to our knowledge, the presence of gas embolism into the coronary arteries has never been reported. We describe the case of a young man who experiences life-threatening gas embolism with the presence of gas bubbles into cardiac cavities and coronary arteries.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
